hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1225","Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Mahdi, who is Ibn Maimun, narrated to us, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Yahya ibn Aqeel, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of Abu Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “One of you will come in the morning, and all my peace be upon him.” It is a charity, for every Tahlil, praise, takbir, and tasbih is a charity, and enjoining what is right and forbidding what is evil is a charity, and it is sufficient for all of that. The two rak'ahs of the forenoon"
